## What changed

**`src/range.ts`** — rewrote `overlaps` plus a small `parse` helper:

- **Touching ranges no longer overlap.** Comparison changed from `<=` to strict `<` (`aStart < bEnd && bStart < aEnd`), reflecting that the end is exclusive.
- **Same start instant still overlaps.** With non-empty ranges, `a.start === b.start` satisfies both strict checks.
- **Zero-length ranges overlap nothing, not even itself.** The plain strict-interval formula would wrongly report an empty range as overlapping any range containing its point, so I return `false` up front when either range has `start === end` (an empty range has no moments to share).
- **Unparseable start or end throws a `TypeError`** whose message includes the offending value (e.g. `` not-a-date does not parse as a date ``). Parse of each field happens before any other check.
- **End before start throws a `RangeError`**, checked after both ranges parse.

**`src/range.test.ts`** — added tests for each rule: touching (both orders), shared start instant, zero-length vs. itself and vs. a containing range, unparseable start/end throwing `TypeError` with the value in the message, and end-before-start throwing `RangeError`.

